    {
      "name": "Respiratory Failure and Hypoxemia",
      "description": "Impaired gas exchange due to lung injury, infection, or acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS) leads to hypoxemia and increased risk of mortality. Key features are low arterial PO2, low SpO2, poor PaO2/FiO2 ratios, high FiO2 requirements, elevated respiratory rate, and reduced respiratory compliance. Severity of hypoxemia directly predicts poor outcomes. Elevated total PEEP and need for significant ventilatory support reflect advanced respiratory compromise.",
