      "name": "Sepsis and Systemic Inflammatory Response",
      "description": "Sepsis triggers a dysregulated host response to infection, resulting in widespread inflammation, endothelial dysfunction, and organ failure. Features such as elevated WBC, C-reactive protein, lactic acid, abnormal temperature, and Sepsis-3 criteria reflect sepsis pathophysiology. Organ dysfunction due to sepsis (as indicated by 'organ_dysfunction' and metabolic derangements) is a strong predictor of ICU mortality.",
