      "description": "Acute kidney injury (AKI) and chronic renal impairment are major contributors to mortality. Elevated BUN, creatinine, BUN/creatinine ratio, and decreased eGFR reflect renal failure and impaired waste excretion. Electrolyte imbalances, such as abnormal sodium, potassium, and calcium levels, can cause arrhythmias, muscle weakness, and further organ dysfunction. Acid-base disturbances, reflected by abnormal arterial pH and bicarbonate, exacerbate morbidity.",
